Operating System Security Governance Program for Unidad Web
Executive Summary

Developed a security governance program for Unidad Web, a cloud services provider supporting more than 5,000 customers. 
The project focused on improving security controls, reducing cyber risk, and supporting compliance requirements across Windows, UNIX, and Linux environments.

Business Problem

Unidad Web stores and processes sensitive customer information and faces risks such as:

Ransomware
Data breaches
Insider threats
Service outages
Unauthorized access

These risks could affect business operations and regulatory compliance.

Project Objectives
Improve system security
Establish governance processes
Strengthen monitoring capabilities
Support regulatory compliance
Reduce operational risk
Environment Overview
Infrastructure
120 Windows 11 workstations
15 Windows Servers
25 Linux Servers
10 UNIX Servers
AWS Cloud Services
Microsoft 365
VPN Infrastructure
Security Architecture

Network diagram:

The environment includes a DMZ, firewall, internal LAN, VPN gateway, and external cloud services.

| Control          | Purpose                     |
| ---------------- | --------------------------- |
| BitLocker        | Data encryption             |
| Windows Defender | Endpoint protection         |
| Group Policy     | Centralized administration  |
| SELinux          | Access control              |
| Tripwire         | File integrity monitoring   |
| Wazuh            | Log analysis and monitoring |
| Snort            | Network intrusion detection |
| Sysmon           | Windows event monitoring    |


These controls were selected using a risk-based approach to improve visibility and protection across the environment.

